## Specifications

- Laravel 12
- PHP 8.3 FPM
- MySQL 8.0
- Redis 8.10.2
- Nginx 1.31.6

## Layer rules

Enforced by `phparkitect.php` (`composer check:architecture`).

- One `{Name}UsecaseInterface` and `{Name}Usecase` per domain, under `Application/{Domain}/Usecases/`. One command per use-case method, under `Application/{Domain}/Commands/`. Controllers construct commands. Use cases accept them and do not take raw arrays.
- `Application` may depend on `App\Domain`, itself, `App\Repositories`, `App\Models`, and vendor classes. It must not depend on `App\Http` or `App\Infrastructure`.
- `Domain` may depend on itself and vendor classes. It must not depend on other `App` layers. Entity classes live under `Domain/{Aggregate}/Entities/`. `App\Domain\Entity` remains the shared base.
- Controllers depend only on a use-case interface and on command classes. They keep HTTP validation, status codes, and API resources. They do not call repositories, Eloquent, or concrete use cases.
- Use cases type-hint repository interfaces, not concrete repositories. Each use-case method accepts one command. They return the same models, `PaginatedResult`, `MapResult`, or null that the controller needs.
- Each domain repository exposes reads and writes for that aggregate, including pivot attaches. Search card repositories stay separate from the aggregate repositories. `SearchCache` stays a repository and model-hook helper; attach-only writes invalidate it inside the repository.
- Ports for external systems stay in Application and are implemented in Infrastructure. Image storage goes through `TemporaryImageStorageInterface`.
- Commands are readonly input objects in `Application/{Domain}/Commands/`. They may depend on `App\Domain`, other application commands and inputs, `App\Models`, and vendor classes. They must not depend on repositories, HTTP, or infrastructure.
- Health, readiness, OpenAPI, and the local admin token route are not domain use cases.
